"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act2_ch12.md — do not edit */

SC["a2c12_open"]={img:"ash",
 t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER TWELVE — UNRAVELED`)+P(`Dawn comes up grey through the broken roof-ring, and the Hall of Quiet Ash is quiet a new way — empty-quiet, ash drifting down through the light like the world's slowest snow, settling on a dead loom, a husk with an iron door in its chest, and you.`)+((G.f.a2_breach=="clean")?(P(`Under the floor, where a furnace pit raged eight hours ago, a patch of new gold lies woven into the mountain's silver veins, holding, humming half a tone brighter than the stone around it. You did that. Nobody alive will ever know how close it came, which is, you are discovering, what victory mostly feels like.`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_breach=="helped")?(P(`Granny Sho sits on the dais steps with her cane across her knees, listening to the mended vein under the floor the way you'd watch a sleeping child. Yan Shuo stands at the door he broke, sword sheathed, composing — you can tell from his face — the formal report of his life. None of you have spoken in an hour. There's a kind of tired that's better than talking.`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_breach=="burned")?(P(`Your left palm aches around its new scar — a thread of true gold laid down the lifeline, fused into the skin, the mountain's receipt for services rendered. It will ache before storms for the rest of your life. Every time, you will think of floodwater, and choose, all over again, to be glad.`)):(""))+P(`The lanterns came down the mountain at dawn. The elders come up it now — six of them, on swords, with the rising sun behind them and forty years of institutional embarrassment waiting in this room, and you stand up in your torn tournament robes to meet the part of the story where being right is not the same as being safe.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`What the elders find is a hall full of evidence and a servant standing over their colleague.`,go:"a2c12_tribunal"}]};

SC["a2c12_tribunal"]={t:()=>P(`They convene on the spot — no public square for this, just six old powers in a ruined hall deciding what the truth is going to be allowed to cost. The reflex you can read on every face is the institution's oldest: <i>bury the embarrassment, and look, the embarrassment is conveniently already standing in a grave.</i>`)+P(`What saves you is testimony, and the witnesses you have are the choices you made.`)+((G.f.yanRespect)?(P(`Yan Shuo testifies first, fist to palm, voice carrying like a struck bell: what he investigated, what he arranged, what he saw through the broken door. An inner-court genius spending his whole accumulated honor on a servant's word, in front of the elders who polished him — and the arithmetic of the room visibly moves.`)):(""))+((G.mei>=3)?(P(`Mei testifies in dosage-instruction voice: the timeline, the herbs, the fines, the bait-pot, each fact laid down like a row of labeled jars. An elder interrupts once. She waits him out with folded hands and resumes one clause earlier than where he stopped her, and he does not interrupt again.`)):(""))+((G.tang>=2)?(P(`And the basement comes up the mountain. Tang at the front with her arms crossed, the kitchens and wash-yards and wood-stations behind her, not testifying so much as <i>attending</i> — two hundred people who feed the sect standing in the dawn cold being visibly owed an outcome. Elders can discount any witness except breakfast.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_leverage)?(P(`Last and strangest: Steward Qiu, unsummoned, with his other ledger under his arm, testifying in a clerk's flat murmur that Elder Kang's accounts have failed to balance for eleven years and that he can show his work. Fear of you has become load-bearing in that man. He does not look at you once, and he buries Kang with columns.`)):(""))+((!G.f.yanRespect&&G.mei<3&&G.tang<2&&!G.f.a1_leverage)?(P(`The trouble is, you spent a year being careful instead of being known, and the room holds exactly one witness: you. The verdict you finally extract is the grudging kind, bought with the ledger and the husk and the undeniable hole in the roof — cleared, recorded, and WATCHED, a file opened somewhere with your name on it in very neat ink.`)):(""))+P(`The verdict, by noon: the servant-disciple acted to preserve the mountain. Sealed record. Which leaves the question the elders want answered before anyone leaves this hall — Kang's ledger, forty years of names and purchases, currently in your hands. Three of the six are already reaching for it.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Surrender it whole. Let the institution own its own shame.`,do:()=>{G.f.a2_ledger="gave";note("The ledger vanishes into the rites office before sundown, sealed, swallowed. You watched one page as it went: the last page. You know what's stamped there.");},go:"a2c12_ruan"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Surrender it — after tonight. One night, one lamp, one memory that doesn't let go.`,req:()=>(G.mind>=6),rq:"(needs Mind 6)",do:()=>{G.f.a2_ledger="copied";addIns(1);note("You read until the lamp dies, and file forty years where no one sweeps. When the rites office seals the original, it seals an empty gesture. The names live in you now. So does the last page.");},go:"a2c12_ruan"},
  {id:"c2",l:`Hand it to Yan Shuo before the elders can ask twice. Honor needs a copy the institution can't bury.`,req:()=>(G.f.yanRespect),rq:"(needs Yan Shuo's oath)",do:()=>{G.f.a2_ledger="yan";G.yan++;note("Yan Shuo +1. He takes it like a drawn blade — formally, both hands, fully aware of the edge. “I'll keep it where honor keeps things,” he says, which you suspect is somewhere genuinely terrifying.");},go:"a2c12_ruan"}]};

SC["a2c12_ruan"]={t:()=>P(`You find Ruan at dusk, because nobody else has thought to look for him, and he is exactly where you knew he'd be: kneeling on the cold floor of the hall, before the dead loom, in the full formal posture of a disciple attending his master's lesson. He has been there all day.`)+P(`“He found me in a famine ditch,” Ruan says, to the loom, not to you. “Weighed me like grain. Fed me, trained me, measured me every season of nineteen years.” The iron veil is gone; what's underneath looks young. “I knew the hall hummed. I never asked what tuned it. A measuring rod that doesn't ask what it measures FOR—” His hands flex once on his knees, and stop.`)+P(`He is the best martial artist of his generation, kneeling in the ashes of the only arithmetic he's ever known, and tomorrow every faction on this mountain will try to pick him up like a dropped sword.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Kneel down next to him. Attend the dead man's last lesson together, as long as it takes.`,do:()=>{G.f.a2_ruan_hand=true;note("You kneel an hour in the cold before he speaks: “You bowed like a servant the day you beat me.” A long pause. “Teach me that.” It is the strangest request anyone has made of you on this mountain, and you understand it completely.");},go:"a2c12_mei"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Leave him the night. Some knots a man has to untie alone.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);},go:"a2c12_mei"}]};

SC["a2c12_mei"]={t:()=>((G.f.a2_mei_bench=="star")?(P(`Mei finds you on the infirmary steps with two bowls of congee and her apprenticeship token already on a cord around her neck, where the basement can see it. “Inner court in spring,” she says, businesslike, and then ruins it by grinning into her bowl. The door in the valley opened, and she walked through it carrying your secret the whole way, and it cost her exactly what it cost and she'd pay it again. Neither of you says any of that. The congee is excellent.`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_mei_bench=="suspect")?(P(`Mei finds you on the infirmary steps with two bowls of congee and a clerk's note, obtained by means she declines to specify, which she burns in the brazier between you without comment. Kang's fall buried every question anyone was storing up about the people near you — her lie is heroism now, officially, retroactively.`)+P(`“So that's settled,” she says, and then sets the boundary with surgical kindness: “I'm not doing it again. The next secret I carry for you, I choose to pick up — you don't get to hand it to me by existing. Agreed?” You agree. It feels less like losing a shield and more like meeting Mei, finally, at her actual height.`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_mei_bench=="robbed")?(P(`Mei finds you on the infirmary steps with two bowls of congee and no token, because the rites-office boy still has her future and Kang's fall un-stole nothing. What she has instead is a plan: the salve, the REAL one, brewed on her grandmother's brazier and sold down-mountain through Bao's chandler contacts, jar by jar, to people who heal faster and don't ask why. “The inner court took the idea,” she says, level as a scale. “It can't take the hands.” Somewhere down the valley her remedy is already outgrowing the sect that wouldn't have her. You did this, partly, with one sensible word. You eat your congee and own it.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`And then there's Bao.`,go:"a2c12_bao"}]};

SC["a2c12_bao"]={t:()=>((G.f.a2_ring=="fed")?(P(`The discipline office's clerk arrives the day after the verdict, because bureaucracy is the one power on this mountain that fears nothing: a row of figures from a wine-shop slate, your matches, foreknowledge priced and itemized, your name running through it like a watermark. The tournament's honor council can't unsee it.`)+P(`Bao is already packing when you find him — for the road, for the down-mountain, for the version of this where he eats it alone. That's the version you cancel.`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_ring=="cold")?(P(`Bao is on the kitchen steps the night after the verdict, in his old spot by the warm chimney, turning his paid-out betting slip over and over — <i>servant survives the sect's hospitality</i>, worst odds on the books, his whole stake, your whole life. He's debt-free. He's still hurt. Both things are true and he is sitting with them the way the basement sits with everything: outside, near the warmth, working.`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_ring=="staked")?(P(`Bao spends the aftermath the way only Bao could: constructing, from a cleared slate and two coppers and a framed third copper, the basement's first honest bookmaking operation — “fixed margins, posted odds, no leg-breakers, an innovation” — and lecturing the wood-yard on probability like a man who didn't nearly drown in it. He pays your pledged purse back to the copper, publicly, with interest he invented for the occasion. You are, he announces, his founding investor. You were not consulted. You are also, you realize, completely fine with it.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Claim it. Your knowledge, your matches, your name on the stain.`,hide:()=>(G.f.a2_ring!="fed"),do:()=>{G.f.a2_stain=true;note("The council strikes your tournament honors from the rite's rolls — the robes stay, the title doesn't. The basement, which knows exactly what you did and for whom, treats the missing title like a medal. Bao doesn't speak for two days, then never stops again.");},go:"a2c12_seal"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Spend the victor's purse buying the slate whole — the ring values silence at exactly market rate.`,hide:()=>(G.f.a2_ring!="fed"),do:()=>{G.f.a2_purse_spent=true;note("Every coin the tournament paid you goes back down two terraces in a sack, and a slate gets wiped in front of two witnesses. You are once again the richest man on the mountain in soup alone. Bao watches you hand his ruin away and ages backward visibly.");},go:"a2c12_seal"},
  {id:"c2",l:`Sit down in your old spot. Let the chimney do the talking until he's ready.`,hide:()=>(G.f.a2_ring!="cold"),do:()=>{G.bao+=2;note("Bao +2. It takes him until moonrise. “You were right to say no,” he says finally, to the chimney. “Hated it. You were right.” A pause. “Bet on you anyway.” That's the whole conversation, and it's enough — it's Bao saying the refusal and the friendship were never the same ledger.");},go:"a2c12_seal"},
  {id:"c3",l:`Leave him the win and the quiet. Some debts shouldn't be collected on.`,hide:()=>(G.f.a2_ring!="cold"),do:()=>{note("You leave him the steps and the slip and the moonrise. Some fences mend faster unwatched. By week's end he's calling you 'your lordship' again, which from Bao is a treaty.");},go:"a2c12_seal"},
  {id:"c4",l:`The mountain settles. One thing doesn't.`,hide:()=>(G.f.a2_ring=="fed"||G.f.a2_ring=="cold"),go:"a2c12_seal"}]};

SC["a2c12_seal"]={img:"seal",
 t:()=>((G.f.a2_ledger=="gave")?(P(`It's the last page that won't leave you alone. You saw it for four seconds as the rites office swallowed the ledger, and four seconds was enough, because you have the kind of memory that doesn't let go:`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_ledger=="copied")?(P(`It's the last page of your midnight copy that stops you cold, three nights after the verdict, when you finally reach the end of forty years:`)):(""))+((G.f.a2_ledger=="yan")?(P(`Yan Shuo comes to you three nights after the verdict, ledger under his arm, walking like a man carrying a live coal. He opens it to the last page without a word:`)):(""))+P(`Receipts. Not entries — <i>receipts</i>, in a different hand, acknowledging tribute RECEIVED. Forty years of them, one per season, each stamped with the same seal: a silkworm, devouring its own cocoon.`)+P(`Kang paid upward. The treasurer had a treasurer. Somewhere off this mountain sits whoever sold a famine-ditch elder a furnace's plans and collected a season-tithe of harvested soul-heat for forty years — and the receipts run to an address that is not on the mountain, written as riverhouse coordinates, the kind merchants use on the waters two valleys down. The Hall of Quiet Ash wasn't an aberration. It was a <i>franchise</i>.`)+((G.sho>=3)?(P(`And one receipt, forty years old, the first, carries a margin note in Kang's younger hand: <i>initial consignment accepted in lieu of fee. Female, local, anomalous resonance. The Court values the rare ones.</i> Local. Anomalous. The mountain didn't eat Wen Suyin. The mountain SHIPPED her.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Winter's snow is gone off the thousand steps. The road down them is open.`,go:"a2c12_curtain"}]};

SC["a2c12_curtain"]={t:()=>P(`Spring opens the mountain like a book, and the mountain, with uncharacteristic timing, offers you everything.`)+P(`The elders — owing you, fearing you, preferring you visible — offer formal rank: inner court, a courtyard of your own, archive rights, a seat at the foot of the table where the sect decides what it is. Real power, real walls, real position to dig from. The basement glows about it for a week. Granny Sho sweeps and says nothing, loudly.`)+P(`And two valleys down, on waters you've never seen, there's a riverhouse address where a silkworm seal collects its season-tithe — and every day you spend behind real walls is a season some other mountain's furnace gets fed.`)+P(`Rank, or the road. The mountain holds its breath politely. You stand at the top of the thousand steps with the spring wind pulling at new robes, and you don't answer it yet — endings deserve mornings, and so do beginnings, and you have, for the first time since a bus shelter in the rain, the luxury of one night to choose.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Sleep on it, at the top of the steps, under the alien stars you've stopped calling alien.`,go:"end_book1"}]};

SC["end_book1"]={img:"title",
 t:()=>`<div class="ending"><h3>END OF BOOK ONE — THE AZURE TRIALS</h3>`+P(`The furnace is cold. The mountain stands. A hundred souls went home, or onward, or wherever the freed go — and somewhere downriver, a silkworm seal is about to learn that its quietest franchise has gone quiet a different way.`)+P(`${G.name}'s story continues in <b>Act III: The Rivers and Lakes</b> — leaving the mountain, the wandering loom, the second furnace, and the first silk on the water.`)+`<p class="small">Realm: <b>${REALMS[G.realm]}</b> · Insight ${G.insight} · Body ${G.body} / Mind ${G.mind} / Heart ${G.heart}</p>`+`</div>`+SYS(`Act Two ends here — but the thread runs on.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Continue to Act III — Down the Thousand Steps`,go:"a3c13_open"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Return to the title screen (your save is kept)`,go:"start"},
  {id:"c2",l:`⁂ Play again from the beginning (erases this save)`,do:()=>{localStorage.removeItem("gthread");G=fresh();},go:"start"}]};